WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.000
For six years, I packed up other people's offices.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.090
I never asked what stayed sealed.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.360
Hedvig Anyanwu is now a doctoral candidate at Slop University.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.770
My thesis follows the crates through four office moves.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.230
What gets packed is what an organisation keeps doing.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.100
And a crate nobody opens

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.150
carries an old priority forward.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.670
From 2027, my School sets its priorities this way.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.130
If a priority won't fit in two crates,

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.459
it doesn't go on the register.

00:00:31.559 --> 00:00:34.346
No doctoral candidate at Slop University has published more,

00:00:34.495 --> 00:00:35.556
or been cited more.

00:00:36.456 --> 00:00:38.126
Eighty-four research outputs.

00:00:38.325 --> 00:00:40.066
Four hundred and fifty-eight citations.

00:00:40.266 --> 00:00:42.716
And an h-index of fifteen.

00:00:43.715 --> 00:00:45.416
I used to tape those crates shut.

00:00:45.715 --> 00:00:47.306
Now I ask what's inside.

00:00:48.505 --> 00:00:49.925
Read her thesis on our website,

00:00:50.075 --> 00:00:51.175
follow us on Bluesky,

00:00:51.325 --> 00:00:52.405
or drop us an email.
